{"blocks":[["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-9301","What it contributes: The best directly relevant Rust LSP reference: workspace/vault indexing, completion, definitions, references, rename, symbols, diagnostics, fuzzy/unindexed block completion, multi-editor support.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Markdown Oxide (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-9523","Specific paths: src/main.rs; src/cli.rs; src/completion/; src/gotodef.rs; src/references.rs; src/rename.rs; src/symbol.rs; src/diagnostics.rs; .agents/skills/testing-neovim/SKILL.md.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Markdown Oxide (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-9729","Relevance: Editor, Core patterns",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Markdown Oxide (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-9767","Looksyk (P1)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-9788","Priority: P1",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Looksyk (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-9806","URL: Looksyk on Codeberg — Looksyk",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Looksyk (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-9897","Language / license / status: Rust backend plus frontend; AGPL; actively documented, but explicitly a hobby project. Official site advertises large-graph indexing and public benchmarks.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Looksyk (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10092","What it contributes: Independent Rust-backed, Markdown-first knowledge platform explicitly optimizing fast indexing of large graphs. Useful for index scheduling, query and performance ideas.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Looksyk (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10288","Specific paths: backend/ first, including its Cargo benchmarks; frontend/looksyk/; official migration_from_logseq/, installation and benchmark/technical-concept docs. Development is centered around the Rust backend.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Looksyk (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10520","Relevance: Core, Bench, Publish ideas",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Looksyk (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10563","Marksman (P1)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10585","Priority: P1",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Marksman (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10603","URL: artempyanykh/marksman",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Marksman (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10679","Language / license / status: F/.NET; MIT; mature, ~3.3k stars, self-contained binaries.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Marksman (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-10778","What it contributes: Mature generic Markdown LSP already solving completion, definitions, references, rename, diagnostics and wiki-link handling. It is the thing garden lsp should coexist with rather than duplicate.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Marksman (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11001","Specific paths: Marksman/; LanguageServerProtocol/; Tests/; Benchmarks/; MarkdigPatches/; .marksman.toml.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Marksman (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11124","Relevance: Editor",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","Marksman (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11147","obsidian.nvim (P1)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11174","Priority: P1",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","obsidian.nvim (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11192","URL: obsidian-nvim/obsidian.nvim",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","obsidian.nvim (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11280","Language / license / status: Lua; Apache-2.0; actively maintained, updated Aug. 2026.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","obsidian.nvim (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11377","What it contributes: Strong Neovim-native precedent for making a Markdown dialect feel native without inventing a separate filetype; current implementation includes an in-process LSP with rename/update-links and PKM actions.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","obsidian.nvim (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11607","Specific paths: lua/obsidian/note.lua; docs/LSP-Progress.md; LSP wiki; follow implementations of definitions, references/backlinks, rename and code actions.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","obsidian.nvim (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11838","Relevance: Editor",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","obsidian.nvim (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11861","publish-spa (P1)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11886","Priority: P1",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","publish-spa (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11904","URL: logseq/publish-spa",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","publish-spa (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-11974","Language / license / status: ClojureScript/Node; MIT; official/current; DB-graph support is explicitly on indefinite hold.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","publish-spa (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12108","What it contributes: Official current file-graph publisher. Important as a publication-semantics oracle, even though its SPA architecture is precisely what you want to escape.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","publish-spa (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12289","Specific paths: src/; publish_spa.mjs; action.yml; nbb.edn; test/.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","publish-spa (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12371","Relevance: Publish, Core oracle",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","publish-spa (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12408","old logseq/publish (P1)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12440","Priority: P1",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","old logseq/publish (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12458","URL: logseq/publish",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","old logseq/publish (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12520","Language / license / status: React/Next.js; historical/early-stage project.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","old logseq/publish (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12607","What it contributes: Earlier Next.js static publisher whose stated motivation was that bundling the whole Logseq web app was slow and not SEO-friendly. Conceptually much closer to the eventual publisher.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","old logseq/publish (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12816","Specific paths: src/components/ — particularly LS* Logseq-specific renderers — and the JSON-to-static-render transformation path.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","old logseq/publish (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12963","Relevance: Publish",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","old logseq/publish (P1)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-12987","nbb-logseq (P2)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13011","Priority: P2",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","nbb-logseq (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13029","URL: logseq/nbb-logseq — Logseq/npm/@logseq/nbb-logseq",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","nbb-logseq (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13135","Language / license / status: ClojureScript/Node; official Logseq project; used by graph-validator and publish-spa.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","nbb-logseq (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13261","What it contributes: Easiest way to script current Logseq ClojureScript/DataScript semantics from Node; useful for generating golden graph fixtures and differential checks.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","nbb-logseq (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13439","Specific paths: nbb.edn; examples around graph scripting; pin graph-parser as a git dependency for oracle tooling.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","nbb-logseq (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13561","Relevance: CLI, Core oracle",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","nbb-logseq (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13594","LogseqLSP (P2)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13617","Priority: P2",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","LogseqLSP (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13635","URL: WhiskeyJack96/logseqlsp",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","LogseqLSP (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13715","Language / license / status: Go; no license detected by GitHub; last code push Nov. 5, 2023, so effectively stale for this project.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","LogseqLSP (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-13852","What it contributes: Historical attempt at a Logseq-aware language server; valuable mainly for seeing which Logseq editor operations somebody thought were worth mapping into LSP.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","LogseqLSP (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14036","Specific paths: main.go; document/; files/; logseq/; lsp.json.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","LogseqLSP (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14114","Relevance: Editor, historical",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","LogseqLSP (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14149","logseq-go (P2)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14172","Priority: P2",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","logseq-go (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14190","URL: aholstenson/logseq-go",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","logseq-go (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14266","Language / license / status: Go; explicitly early-development and warns that modification may destroy data.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","logseq-go (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14385","What it contributes: Useful future mutation/API precedent: page rename/delete, reference updates, linked references, block lookup, aliases and namespaces.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","logseq-go (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14545","Specific paths: Root graph model, watcher code (watcher.go), page/block mutation and reference-update implementations.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","logseq-go (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14671","Relevance: CLI/mutation reference",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","logseq-go (P2)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-14710","The ordering matters. lsdoc / mldoc / graph-parser answer correctness questions; Tine answers many engine questions; Markdown/Oxide answers many LSP questions. Looksyk is worth studying after those rather than before them because its migration guide documents semantic differences from Logseq: tags may need conversion from #tag to double-bracket page links, queries use a different syntax, TODOs can be migrated to checkbox form, and nested assets are not indexed.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-15202","There is also an operational mismatch between Looksyk and the design constraints: its documented Docker path exposes a backend on port 11000. That does not make its indexing code uninteresting; it is simply a reason not to inherit its runtime/service boundary.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-15477","The current Logseq product split makes the official OG code especially valuable as a fixed compatibility target. Logseq announced on April 24, 2026 that file-based Markdown graphs moved to logseq/og, while the main logseq/logseq product became the database-graph line. This supports the framing already in the Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Brief: Logseq/OG behavior should be a compatibility target, not an application dependency.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-15946","Public benchmark gardens",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-15977","A practical finding from this research is that truly large, openly available, Git-backed Logseq/OG gardens are not abundant. Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-encode-garden is substantially more interesting as a scale benchmark than the public examples verified; the official docs graph and Pengx's garden are more valuable as correctness/publishing diversity tests.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-16352","codekiln/logseq-encode-garden",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-16390","Repository: codekiln/logseq-encode-garden — Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-encode-garden",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","codekiln/logseq-encode-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-16541","Published site: codekiln.github.io/logseq-encode-garden",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","codekiln/logseq-encode-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-16654","Verified approximate size: 4,968 pages/*.md + 507 journals/*.md ≈ 5,475 Markdown files. GitHub code search also finds id:: in 318 Markdown files.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","codekiln/logseq-encode-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-16813","Notable features / value: Real journals, explicit UUID-bearing content, namespaces/file-name encoding, aliases/properties/references, extensive accumulated real-world material, agent-edited content and an existing publication workload. These are exactly the characteristics called out in the Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Brief.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","codekiln/logseq-encode-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17168","Why benchmark it: Primary performance corpus. Large enough to expose startup/index/cache problems; also exercises actual editor, agent and publishing workloads.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","codekiln/logseq-encode-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17334","Official Logseq docs graph",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17369","Repository: logseq/docs",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","Official Logseq docs graph"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17432","Published site: docs.logseq.com",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","Official Logseq docs graph"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17497","Verified approximate size: GitHub currently indexes about 210 Markdown files under pages/.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","Official Logseq docs graph"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17595","Notable features / value: First-party graph whose publishing pipeline is explicitly cited by publish-spa; naturally contains broad Logseq syntax/documentation examples.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","Official Logseq docs graph"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17775","Why benchmark it: Primary compatibility canary. Small enough for exhaustive comparison; official enough that parser differences deserve investigation.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","Official Logseq docs graph"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17931","pengx17/knowledge-garden",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-17964","Repository: pengx17/knowledge-garden",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","pengx17/knowledge-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-18053","Published site: pengx17.github.io/knowledge-garden",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","pengx17/knowledge-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-18156","Verified approximate size: About 160 Markdown page files by GitHub code search; repository tree also contains a substantial collection of Logseq-style assets including PDFs/media.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","pengx17/knowledge-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-18341","Notable features / value: Older real-life public Logseq garden with media/assets and an established published form.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","pengx17/knowledge-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-18462","Why benchmark it: Publishing regression corpus. Not a scale benchmark, but useful for avoiding an implementation accidentally tailored only to one graph.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens","pengx17/knowledge-garden"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-18621","Also manufacture synthetic stress gardens, because a real garden gives ecological validity but poor control. A generator should be able to produce, for example, 10k/50k/100k pages with controlled fan-out, namespace depth, explicit-UUID density, journals, heavily referenced hub pages and block-ref chains. That lets you answer whether an index has O(n) versus hidden O(n²) behavior rather than merely observing that one real graph was \"fast enough.\" lsdoc itself takes this philosophy seriously: its project explicitly runs adversarial performance and stack-overflow gates in addition to correctness differentials.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-19243","Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-encode-garden should nevertheless remain the release acceptance corpus. Its current repo was pushed on September 12, 2026 and its configured homepage is the current published garden, making it a living rather than archival workload.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Public benchmark gardens"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-19514","Fork, adapt, or build new",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-19546","Recommendation: new project, selectively adapted dependencies/reference implementations.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-19643","logseq-gardener itself",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-19674","Recommendation: NEW PROJECT",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","logseq-gardener itself"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-19711","Rationale: None of the existing projects has the exact product boundary: one read-first semantic engine shared by a CLI/agents, stdio LSP and page-oriented static publisher, with Markdown authoritative and no mandatory daemon. That boundary is the core insight in the Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Brief.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","logseq-gardener itself"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-20042","lsdoc",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-20056","Recommendation: ADAPT / PIN / possibly vendor a local fork",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","lsdoc"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-20124","Rationale: This may eliminate the highest-risk task—faithfully parsing Logseq Markdown—without forcing Tine's application architecture on you. Its public API is intentionally consumable as a Cargo dependency and provides source spans plus refs/outline APIs.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","lsdoc"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-20391","mldoc",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-20405","Recommendation: ADAPT AS ORACLE; fork only if Proposal C wins",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","mldoc"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-20476","Rationale: It is canonical and now has a highly relevant fast parse_outline_only path. But making it the production core means accepting an OCaml core or an FFI/process boundary.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new","mldoc"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-20667","Logseq OG graph-parser",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Fork, adapt, or build new"]]],"format_version":5}